  "generated_text": "Let's review and correct the solution step by step.\n\nGiven the parametric equations:\n\\[\nx(t) = 3t^2 - 9t - 5\n\\]\n\\[\ny(t) = t^2 - 3t + 2\n\\]\n\nWe need to find the arc length \\(L\\) of the curve from \\(t = 0\\) to \\(t = 4\\).\n\nFirst, compute the derivatives:\n\\[\n\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(3t^2 - 9t - 5) = 6t - 9\n\\]\n\\[\n\\frac{dy}{dt} = \\frac{d}{dt}(t^2 - 3t + 2) = 2t - 3\n\\]\n\nThe arc length formula is:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{dx}{dt}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nSubstitute the derivatives:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^4 \\sqrt{(6t - 9)^2 + (2t - 3)^2} \\, dt\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression inside the square root:\n\\[\n(6t - 9)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81\n\\]\n\\[\n(2t - 3)^2 = 4t^2 - 12t + 9\n\\]\n\nAdd these two expressions:\n\\[\n(6t - 9)^2 + (2t - 3)^2 = 36t^2 - 108t + 81 + 4t^2 - 12t + 9 = 40t^2 - 120t + 90\n\\]\n\nFactor out the common term:\n\\[\n40t^2 - 120t + 90 = 10(4t^2 - 12t + 9) = 10(2t - 3)^2\n\\]\n\nThus, the integrand simplifies to:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{10(2t - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{10} \\cdot |2t - 3|\n\\]\n\nSince \\(0 \\le t \\le 4\\), we need to consider the intervals where \\(2t - 3\\) is positive and negative. Specifically:\n- For \\(0 \\le t \\le 1.5\\), \\(2t - 3 \\le 0\\), so \\(|2t - 3| = 3 - 2t\\).\n- For \\(1.5 < t \\le 4\\), \\(2t - 3 > 0\\), so \\(|2t - 3| = 2t - 3\\).\n\nThus, the integrand becomes:\n\\[\n\\sqrt{10} (3 - 2t) \\quad \\text{for} \\quad 0 \\le t \\le 1.5\n\\]\n\\[\n\\sqrt{10} (2t - 3) \\quad \\text{for} \\quad 1.5 < t \\le 4\n\\]\n\nNow, we split the integral:\n\\[\nL = \\int_0^{1.5} \\sqrt{10} (3 - 2t) \\, dt + \\int_{1.5}^4 \\sqrt{10} (2t - 3) \\, dt\n\\]\n\nEvaluate each integral separately.\n\nFor the first integral:\n\\[\n\\int_0^{1.5} \\sqrt{10} (3 - 2t) \\, dt = \\sqrt{10} \\int_0^{1.5} (3 - 2t) \\, dt\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{10} \\left[ 3t - t^2 \\right]_0^{1.5} = \\sqrt{10} \\left[ (3 \\cdot 1.5 - (1.5)^2) - (0) \\right]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{10} \\left[ 4.5 - 2.25 \\right] = \\sqrt{10} \\cdot 2.25 = 2.25\\sqrt{10}\n\\]\n\nFor the second integral:\n\\[\n\\int_{1.5}^4 \\sqrt{10} (2t - 3) \\, dt = \\sqrt{10} \\int_{1.5}^4 (2t - 3) \\, dt\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{10} \\left[ t^2 - 3t \\right]_{1.5}^4 = \\sqrt{10} \\left[ (4^2 - 3 \\cdot 4) - (1.5^2 - 3 \\cdot 1.5) \\right]\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{10} \\left[ (16 - 12) - (2.25 - 4.5) \\right] = \\sqrt{10} \\left[ 4 - (-2.25) \\right] = \\sqrt{10} \\cdot 6.25 = 6.25\\sqrt{10}\n\\]\n\nFinally, sum the results:\n\\[\nL = 2.25\\sqrt{10} + 6.25\\sqrt{10} = 8.5\\sqrt{10}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of the paint trail left by the tennis ball is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{8.5\\sqrt{10}}\n\\]",
